# Jaguar E-type Series 2 fixed-head coupe, 1968-1971.
#
# The Series 2: open headlamps, larger below-bumper indicators, a wrap-around
# rear bumper with the lamps below it and an enlarged grille. The fixed-head
# coupe is modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar_E-Type
#
# Dimensions 4.453 x 1.657 x 1.222 m, wheelbase 2.438 m. The Series 1 figures
# are carried over; no separate Series 2 table was sighted, and the pack says
# so rather than implying a second source.
#
# Shape reference: a true level side elevation of a black 1969 car, plus front
# and rear three-quarters and a detail.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no period UK document was sighted. Cream, Signal Red,
# Black and British Racing Green are period Jaguar names recorded as context.
# Weights 5, 4, 3, 2, total 14, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 230 km/h. Comfort 62/423, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 62. Classes 3,4.
# Dates October 1968 to 1971 production, road tail staggered 1982-1984.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/jaguar-e-type-s2.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/jaguar-e-type-s2.dae. References:
# citycars/references/jaguar-e-type-s2/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: built as a variant of the Series 1 4.2 master with the
# open headlamps, larger indicators, wrap-around rear bumper and enlarged grille.
# The side photograph is oblique (from the rear), so the comparison camera was
# matched to it rather than treated as a true elevation. Lamp and bumper detail
# is simplified at sprite scale.


obj=citycar
name=JaguarETypeS2(Cream)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=5
intro_year=1968
intro_month=10
retire_year=1984
retire_month=6
speed=230
class=3,4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=62
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=423

